    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0443" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg349"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Lincoln.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-02-04"><hi rendition="#italic">February 4,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1049.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch, No. 897, of the
                    13th ultimo, relative to the restrictions upon the admission of American cattle
                    into Canada, I inclose for your information a copy of a letter dated the 2d
                    instant, from the Secretary of Agriculture, reviewing in detail the grounds upon
                    which this Government claims that this country is now entirely free from
                    pleuro-pneumonia.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to communicate the purport of Mr. Rusk’s letter to the foreign
                    office.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Foster.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d267-a1.xml" xpointer="d267-a1"/>
